---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookies — CleanerBath"
  description="CleanerBath cookies policy. Short version: we don't use any tracking or advertising cookies."
>
  <header class="border-b border-sage-100 bg-cream-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 sm:px-8 py-5">
      <a href="/" class="text-sage-700 text-sm hover:underline">← Back to CleanerBath</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 sm:px-8 py-16">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-sage-700 font-semibold">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold">Cookies</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-700/70">Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' })}</p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">Short version</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700/85 leading-relaxed">
      CleanerBath doesn't use any analytics, advertising, or tracking cookies. We don't load Google Analytics,
      Meta Pixel, TikTok Pixel, or any other third-party scripts. The site is fully usable without cookies.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">What we do store</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700/85 leading-relaxed">
      The site itself is a static HTML/CSS/JS bundle. When you submit the lead form, your form data is sent via HTTPS
      to our form-handling service (Formspree by default). That's it — no first-party cookies, no session IDs, no
      fingerprinting.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Server logs</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700/85 leading-relaxed">
      Our hosting provider (Netlify) records standard request logs: your IP address, the page you visited, the response code,
      and the user-agent string. These logs are kept for up to 30 days for security and capacity planning, then deleted.
      They are not used for marketing.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">If we add analytics later</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700/85 leading-relaxed">
      If we add analytics in the future (for example Plausible, which is cookieless), we'll update this page.
      We will never add invasive tracking, advertising cookies, or third-party data-sharing without your explicit consent.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700/85 leading-relaxed">
      Questions about cookies or privacy? Use the contact form on our home page.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>